{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KhPgNWbf69QtDkVcUPtpWY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `picoquic/bytestream.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! A small cursor-over-buffer helper used by `logwriter.c` /\n4\t//! `logreader.c` (binlog) and the connection-id encoding paths.\n5\t//! Three storage modes share a single [`ByteStream`] type:\n6\t//!\n7\t//! * **Borrowed** — wrap a caller-owned slice via\n8\t//!   [`ByteStream::from_slice`].  C: `bytestream_ref_init`.\n9\t//! * **Inline** — a stack-allocated [`ByteStreamBuf`] holds 2560\n10\t//!   bytes of inline storage; [`ByteStreamBuf::stream`] hands out a\n11\t//!   [`ByteStream`] borrowing from it.  C: `bytestream_buf` +\n12\t//!   `bytestream_buf_init`.\n13\t//! * **Owned** — [`ByteStream::with_capacity`] returns a\n14\t//!   `ByteStream<'static>` that owns its heap buffer.  C:\n15\t//!   `bytestream_alloc` + `bytestream_delete` (the latter folds\n16\t//!   into `Drop`).\n17\t//!\n18\t//! ## Shape choices\n19\t//!\n20\t//! C: `bytestream { uint8_t* data; size_t size; size_t ptr; }`.\n21\t//! Rust: `ByteStream<'a> { data: ByteStreamData<'a>, ptr: usize }`.\n22\t//! `data` collapses the C `(uint8_t*, size_t)` pair into one slice\n23\t//! whose `.len()` subsumes `size`; the enum variant distinguishes\n24\t//! borrowed from owned storage so all three constructors produce\n25\t//! the same type.\n26\t//!\n27\t//! C `bytestream_buf { bytestream s; uint8_t buf[2560]; }` aliased\n28\t//! `s.data` against `buf` after init — a self-referential pair.\n29\t//! The Rust shape avoids that: [`ByteStreamBuf`] is just storage,\n30\t//! and [`ByteStreamBuf::stream`] returns a `ByteStream<'_>`\n31\t//! borrowing from the inline buffer for the duration of one I/O\n32\t//! pass.\n33\t//!\n34\t//! Operations are methods on [`ByteStream`].  C `int` 0/-1 returns\n35\t//! become `Result<T, Error>`; out-parameters fold into the `Ok`\n36\t//! variant (e.g., C `int byteread_int8(bytestream*, uint8_t*)`\n37\t//! becomes `fn read_u8(&mut self) -> Result<u8, Error>`).\n38\t//!\n39\t//! Phase 4: all function bodies are implemented.\n40\t\n41\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n42\t\n43\tuse crate::ConnectionId;\n44\tuse crate::Error;\n45\t\n46\t/// Inline-buffer capacity carried by [`ByteStreamBuf`].  C:\n47\t/// `BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE`.\n48\tpub const BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE: usize = 2560;\n49\t\n50\t/// Wire-format family tag for IPv4 (matches Linux AF_INET = 2).\n51\tconst WIRE_AF_INET: u64 = 2;\n52\t/// Wire-format family tag for IPv6 (matches Linux AF_INET6 = 10).\n53\tconst WIRE_AF_INET6: u64 = 10;\n54\t\n55\t/// Backing storage for a [`ByteStream`].\n56\t///\n57\t/// An enum so that all three C constructors (ref / buf / alloc)\n58\t/// produce a single [`ByteStream`] type rather than splitting into\n59\t/// \"borrowed\" and \"owned\" variants.\n60\tpub enum ByteStreamData<'a> {\n61\t    /// Slice borrowed from external storage — caller-supplied\n62\t    /// buffer ([`ByteStream::from_slice`]) or the inline buffer of\n63\t    /// a [`ByteStreamBuf`] ([`ByteStreamBuf::stream`]).\n64\t    Borrowed(&'a mut [u8]),\n65\t    /// Heap-allocated buffer owned by the bytestream.  Used by\n66\t    /// [`ByteStream::with_capacity`].  Freed by the [`Drop`] impl\n67\t    /// on the vector — replaces the explicit `bytestream_delete`\n68\t    /// call in C.\n69\t    Owned(Vec<u8>),\n70\t}\n71\t\n72\t/// Cursor over a byte buffer.  C: `bytestream`.\n73\t///\n74\t/// The cursor advances monotonically as bytes are read or written.\n75\t/// `data.len()` (under whichever variant) corresponds to the C\n76\t/// `size` field; the cursor offset corresponds to the C `ptr`\n77\t/// field.\n78\t// Fields are private (encapsulated).  The dead_code allow suppresses\n79\t// warnings until all outer consumers are wired in.\n80\t#[allow(dead_code)]\n81\tpub struct ByteStream<'a> {\n82\t    data: ByteStreamData<'a>,\n83\t    ptr: usize,\n84\t}\n85\t\n86\t/// Inline 2560-byte storage for a stack-allocated bytestream.\n87\t/// C: `bytestream_buf`.\n88\t///\n89\t/// Pair with [`ByteStreamBuf::stream`] to get a usable cursor:\n90\t///\n91\t/// ```ignore\n92\t/// let mut buf = ByteStreamBuf::default();\n93\t/// let s = buf.stream(128).unwrap();\n94\t/// // …read/write through `s`…\n95\t/// ```\n96\t///\n97\t/// Unlike the C struct this does not embed a `bytestream` field;\n98\t/// the cursor lives in the [`ByteStream`] returned by\n99\t/// [`stream`](Self::stream), borrowing from this inline buffer.\n100\t// See `ByteStream` for the rationale on the dead-code allow."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"621e8ef5-6ea2-41f7-92c8-884ed614789d","uuid":"5653f6a4-3bf6-44ea-a4c2-929a581a891f","timestamp":"2026-05-06T12:23:00.222Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/bytestream.rs","content":"//! Translation of `picoquic/bytestream.h`.\n//!\n//! A small cursor-over-buffer helper used by `logwriter.c` /\n//! `logreader.c` (binlog) and the connection-id encoding paths.\n//! Three storage modes share a single [`ByteStream`] type:\n//!\n//! * **Borrowed** — wrap a caller-owned slice via\n//!   [`ByteStream::from_slice`].  C: `bytestream_ref_init`.\n//! * **Inline** — a stack-allocated [`ByteStreamBuf`] holds 2560\n//!   bytes of inline storage; [`ByteStreamBuf::stream`] hands out a\n//!   [`ByteStream`] borrowing from it.  C: `bytestream_buf` +\n//!   `bytestream_buf_init`.\n//! * **Owned** — [`ByteStream::with_capacity`] returns a\n//!   `ByteStream<'static>` that owns its heap buffer.  C:\n//!   `bytestream_alloc` + `bytestream_delete` (the latter folds\n//!   into `Drop`).\n//!\n//! ## Shape choices\n//!\n//! C: `bytestream { uint8_t* data; size_t size; size_t ptr; }`.\n//! Rust: `ByteStream<'a> { data: ByteStreamData<'a>, ptr: usize }`.\n//! `data` collapses the C `(uint8_t*, size_t)` pair into one slice\n//! whose `.len()` subsumes `size`; the enum variant distinguishes\n//! borrowed from owned s