{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Af7dqhUvq5KdgVMvDJaNyn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CeHe2PYo56spTTBP9vsa6Y","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/logger.rs","limit":150},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2284,"cache_read_input_tokens":48016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2284,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016DZDUH2eYQjeMuJdCzNWgY","session_id":"621e8ef5-6ea2-41f7-92c8-884ed614789d","uuid":"eced526c-ae5b-463c-a26a-6531289591f0"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CeHe2PYo56spTTBP9vsa6Y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/unified_log.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Logging API.  The quic library can produce three complementary\n4\t//! logs per QUIC context — a textual trace (see [`crate::textlog`]),\n5\t//! a structured binary trace (see [`crate::binlog`]), and a qlog\n6\t//! (see [`crate::qlog`]) — but most applications only enable a\n7\t//! subset.  Each backend is described by a single [`Logger`] trait\n8\t//! object that the application optionally installs on the QUIC\n9\t//! context.  Per-connection dispatch happens through the [`Log`]\n10\t//! trait (implemented on [`Connection`]); per-context dispatch\n11\t//! happens through inherent methods on [`Quic`].  Either layer\n12\t//! fans the event out to whichever backends are registered.\n13\t//!\n14\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every body is `todo!()`.\n15\t//!\n16\t//! Pointer-shape and translation policy notes for this module:\n17\t//!\n18\t//! * The C `picoquic_unified_logging_t` is a 16-slot vtable.  Per\n19\t//!   the Phase 1 rule \"function pointers map to traits\" we collapse\n20\t//!   the whole vtable into a single trait, [`Logger`],\n21\t//!   because every backend installs all sixteen entries together.\n22\t//!   A QUIC context will eventually hold three optional\n23\t//!   `Box<dyn Logger>` slots (`text_log_fns` / `bin_log_fns`\n24\t//!   / `qlog_fns`); that restructuring lands when `internal.h` is\n25\t//!   translated.\n26\t//! * `Quic*` / `Connection*` — every observed caller passes a non-NULL\n27\t//!   pointer and the logger callbacks may mutate internal state.\n28\t//!   Free functions keyed on `Quic*` become inherent methods on\n29\t//!   [`Quic`]; those keyed on `Connection*` become methods on the\n30\t//!   [`Log`] trait (implemented for [`Connection`]).\n31\t//! * `Path*` — non-NULL for every per-path log event except\n32\t//!   [`Logger::dropped_packet`] and\n33\t//!   [`Logger::packet`], where `packet.c` may pass NULL when\n34\t//!   the path lookup failed.  Those two get `Option<&mut Path>`; the\n35\t//!   rest get `&mut Path`.\n36\t//! * `ConnectionId*` — `dcid` in [`Logger::packet_lost`] is\n37\t//!   nullable per `loss_recovery.c` (the call site explicitly\n38\t//!   substitutes NULL when no remote CID is known); the `cid`\n39\t//!   parameter to [`Logger::quic_app_message`] is always\n40\t//!   non-NULL and read-only.  `Option<&ConnectionId>` and\n41\t//!   `&ConnectionId` respectively.\n42\t//! * `struct sockaddr*` → `&core::net::SocketAddr`, matching the\n43\t//!   convention established in [`crate`].\n44\t//! * `va_list` / variadic — collapsed to [`core::fmt::Arguments`].\n45\t//!   The C `_v` variants disappear: the `format_args!` macro at the\n46\t//!   call site is the Rust substitute for both the variadic and the\n47\t//!   `va_list` flavours.\n48\t//! * `int receiving` / `int is_local` — pure 0/1 flags, promoted to\n49\t//!   `bool`.\n50\t//! * `const uint8_t* + size_t` pairs collapse to `&[u8]`; a NULL\n51\t//!   pointer with len 0 in C maps cleanly to an empty Rust slice.\n52\t//! * `picoquic_log_dropped_packet`'s `raw_data` parameter is\n53\t//!   `UNUSED` in the C wrapper and never reaches the trait, so it is\n54\t//!   dropped from the Rust API entirely.\n55\t\n56\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n57\t\n58\tuse crate::Instant;\n59\tuse crate::internal::{PacketHeader, PacketType};\n60\tuse crate::{Connection, ConnectionId, Path, Quic};\n61\t\n62\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n63\t// Unified-logger vtable.\n64\t//\n65\t// One trait covers all sixteen function-pointer slots of\n66\t// `picoquic_unified_logging_t`.  Every concrete logger (text /\n67\t// binary / qlog) implements the full trait — the C source enforces\n68\t// \"if a logging type is documented, all three functions for that\n69\t// type shall be documented as well\" by convention; the trait\n70\t// requirement makes that explicit.\n71\t//\n72\t// Method names drop the `log_` prefix from the C function-pointer\n73\t// typedefs since the trait name already conveys \"logging\".\n74\t\n75\t/// One installable logging backend.  Each method emits one record\n76\t/// of the named kind into whatever sink the backend owns (text\n77\t/// file, binary trace, qlog).\n78\tpub trait Logger {\n79\t    /// Emit a free-form application message routed by a connection-id\n80\t    /// hint rather than a live `Connection` handle.  C:\n81\t    /// `picoquic_log_quic_app_message_fn`.\n82\t    fn quic_app_message(\n83\t        &mut self,\n84\t        quic: &mut Quic,\n85\t        cid: &ConnectionId,\n86\t        args: core::fmt::Arguments<'_>,\n87\t    );\n88\t\n89\t    /// Emit a context-level UDP-datagram arrival or departure for\n90\t    /// an unknown connection.  C: `picoquic_log_quic_pdu_fn`.\n91\t    fn quic_pdu(\n92\t        &mut self,\n93\t        quic: &mut Quic,\n94\t        receiving: bool,\n95\t        current_time: Instant,\n96\t        cid64: u64,\n97\t        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n98\t        addr_local: &SocketAddr,\n99\t        packet_length: usize,\n100\t    );\n101\t\n102\t    /// Release any QUIC-context-level resource the backend owns\n103\t    /// (file handles, qlog buffers, …).  Invoked at context\n104\t    /// teardown.  C: `picoquic_log_quic_close`.\n105\t    fn quic_close(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic);\n106\t\n107\t    /// Emit a free-form application message attached to a live\n108\t    /// connection.  C: `picoquic_log_app_message_fn` — the `va_list`\n109\t    /// flavour collapses to [`core::fmt::Arguments`].\n110\t    fn app_message(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection, args: core::fmt::Arguments<'_>);\n111\t\n112\t    /// Emit a per-connection UDP-datagram arrival or departure\n113\t    /// record.  C: `picoquic_log_pdu_fn`.\n114\t    fn pdu(\n115\t        &mut self,\n116\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n117\t        receiving: bool,\n118\t        current_time: Instant,\n119\t        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n120\t        addr_local: &SocketAddr,\n121\t        packet_length: usize,\n122\t        unique_path_id: u64,\n123\t        ecn: u8,\n124\t    );\n125\t\n126\t    /// Emit a decrypted-packet record.  `receiving == true` for\n127\t    /// arrivals.  C: `picoquic_log_packet_fn`.\n128\t    fn packet(\n129\t        &mut self,\n130\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n131\t        path_x: Option<&mut Path>,\n132\t        receiving: bool,\n133\t        current_time: Instant,\n134\t        ph: &PacketHeader,\n135\t        bytes: &[u8],\n136\t    );\n137\t\n138\t    /// Emit a record that the packet was dropped due to some error.\n139\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_dropped_packet_fn`.\n140\t    fn dropped_packet(\n141\t        &mut self,\n142\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n143\t        path_x: Option<&mut Path>,\n144\t        ph: &PacketHeader,\n145\t        packet_size: usize,\n146\t        err: i32,\n147\t        current_time: Instant,\n148\t    );\n149\t\n150\t    /// Emit a record that the packet was buffered waiting for"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016DZDUH2eYQjeMuJdCzNWgY","session_id":"621e8ef5-6ea2-41f7-92c8-884ed614789d","uuid":"f2312b67-d578-4e97-bf0e-79e1070f6ec5","timestamp":"2026-05-06T12:24:12.026Z"}
