{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0133bok8t3PA2CFvmtw8tqJP","type":"tool_result","content":"908\tpub trait AutoQlog {\n909\t    fn run(&mut self, connection: &Connection) -> i32;\n910\t}\n911\t\n912\t/// C: `performance_log_fn` — emit a per-connection\n913\t/// performance log row.  `should_delete` is `true` on connection\n914\t/// teardown.  Callback is read-only over `quic` / `connection`.\n915\tpub trait PerformanceLog {\n916\t    fn emit(&mut self, quic: &Quic, connection: &Connection, should_delete: bool) -> i32;\n917\t}\n918\t\n919\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n920\t// Memlog hook (per-connection memory-log callback on `Connection`).\n921\t\n922\t/// C: `void (*memlog_call_back)(Connection*, Path*,\n923\t/// void* v_memlog, int op_code, uint64_t current_time)` field on\n924\t/// `Connection`.  Read-only over `connection`; the path may\n925\t/// mutate (the C body updates per-path counters).\n926\tpub trait MemLogHook {\n927\t    fn callback(\n928\t        &mut self,\n929\t        connection: &Connection,\n930\t        path: &mut Path,\n931\t        op_code: i32,\n932\t        current_time: Instant,\n933\t    );\n934\t}\n935\t\n936\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n937\t// QUIC context.\n938\t\n939\t/// Top-level QUIC context.  C: `Quic`.  Single-threaded\n940\t/// scope (per the translation plan): no `Send`/`Sync`.\n941\tpub struct Quic {\n942\t    /// Client-side TLS configuration (set when this `Quic` is\n943\t    /// being used to make outbound connections).  Replaces the C\n944\t    /// `tls_master_ctx` opaque handle for the client role.\n945\t    pub tls_client_config: Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::DynClientConfig>>,\n946\t    /// Server-side TLS configuration (set when this `Quic` is\n947\t    /// being used to accept inbound connections)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016DZDUH2eYQjeMuJdCzNWgY","session_id":"621e8ef5-6ea