{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014pNApRkpCCG3p6LxCoS3o7","type":"tool_result","content":"3670\t    pub fn primary_path_current_spin(&self) -> bool {\n3671\t        self.paths.first().map(|p| p.current_spin).unwrap_or(false)\n3672\t    }\n3673\t\n3674\t    /// Emit a \"new connection\" log record via both the binlog and text\n3675\t    /// logger backends attached to this connection.\n3676\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_new_connection(cnx)`.\n3677\t    pub fn log_new_connection(&mut self) {\n3678\t        // C: dispatches to text_log_fns / bin_log_fns / qlog_fns on\n3679\t        // cnx->quic when each handle is non-NULL.  Connection has no\n3680\t        // back-reference to Quic under the settled signature, so the\n3681\t        // dispatch reduces to whatever connection-local state has\n3682\t        // been wired by the active backend.  With the loglib backends\n3683\t        // out of v1 scope (per TRANSLATE_PLAN.md), no Logger impls\n3684\t        // attach themselves yet — the C path itself is a no-op for an\n3685\t        // unconfigured context, which is the state we mirror here.\n3686\t        let _ = self.f_binlog.as_ref();\n3687\t        let _ = self.qlog_ctx.as_ref();\n3688\t    }\n3689\t\n3690\t    /// Emit a free-form application message on this connection's log.\n3691\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_app_message(cnx, \"%s\", msg)`.\n3692\t    pub fn log_app_message(&mut self, msg: &str) {\n3693\t        // Same dispatch model as log_new_connection — see that doc\n3694\t        // comment for the Quic / loglib-scope rationale.  The message\n3695\t        // is consumed via the connection-local handles; with no\n3696\t        // backend installed, the call is a no-op, matching the C\n3697\t        // dispatch when text_log_fns / bin_log_fns / qlog_fns are all\n3698\t        // NULL.\n3699\t        let _ = (msg, self.f_binlog.as_ref(), self.qlog_ctx.as_ref());\n3700\t    }\n3701\t}\n3702\t\n3703\t#[cfg(test)]\n3704\tmod test {}\n3705\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"621e8ef5-6ea2-41f7-92c8-884ed614789d","uuid":"70d31cdf-4e00-45bb-8912-2c9cc826d4be","timestamp":"2026-05-06T12:28:59.175Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/lib.rs","content":"    pub fn primary_path_current_spin(&self) -> bool {\n        self.paths.first().map(|p| p.current_spin).unwrap_or(false)\n    }\n\n    /// Emit a \"new connection\" log record via both the binlog and text\n    /// logger backends attached to this connection.\n    /// C: `picoquic_log_new_connection(cnx)`.\n    pub fn log_new_connection(&mut self) {\n        // C: dispatches to text_log_fns / bin_log_fns / qlog_fns on\n        // cnx->quic when each handle is non-NULL.  Connection has no\n        // back-reference to Quic under the settled signature, so the\n        // dispatch reduces to whatever connection-local state has\n        // been wired by the active backend.  With the loglib backends\n        // out of v1 scope (per TRANSLATE_PLAN.md), no Logger impls\n        // attach themselves yet — the C path itself is a no-op for an\n        // unconfigured context, which is the state we mirror here.\n        let _ = self.f_binlog.as_ref();\n        let _ = self.qlog_ctx.as_ref();\n    }\n\n    /// Emit a free-form application message on this connection's log.\n    /// C: `picoquic_log_app_message(cnx, \"%s\", msg)`.\n    pub fn log_app_message(&mut self, msg: &str) {\n        // Same dispatch model as log_new_connection — see that doc\n        // comment for the Quic / loglib-scope rationale.  The message\n        // is consumed via the connection-local handles; with no\n        // backend installed, the call is a no-op, matching the C\n        // dispatch when text_log_fns / bin_log_fns / qlog_fns are all\n        // NULL.\n        let _ = (msg, self.f_binlog.as_ref(), self.qlog_ctx.as_ref());\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod test {}\n","numLines":36,"startLine":3670,"totalLi